  data: {
    LLM: "Play 2s and Jokers last—they're your highest cards and can always beat any play. Never waste them early.\n\nHand Shape: Analyze how many singles, pairs, and sequences you hold. If opponents are playing pairs, hold your pairs for later responses. Sequence play can empty 4-6 cards in one turn.\n\nRevolution Timing: Playing a four-of-a-kind revolution at the right moment can completely flip the power dynamic when you hold a lot of low cards. Track who has how many cards—fewer remaining cards = that player is close to ending the round.",
